// Applied to EVERY target in a build, Swift packages included, by pointing the
// XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE environment variable at this file. It is not included by
// any target, and must not be: a target's xcconfig never reaches package
// targets, which is the whole reason this file exists (DECISIONS.md, 2026-11-07).
//
// What it buys: -Osize on remote packages that no manifest here can configure.
// GRDB alone drops 2,144 -> 1,570 KB; the phone binary 5.51 -> 4.73 MB, and the
// watch app ~1.2 MB.
//
// Where it is set:
//   - Xcode Cloud: an environment variable on the TestFlight workflow,
//     XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE = /Volumes/workspace/repository/HolmdelApp/Config/Shipping.xcconfig
//     (ci_scripts/ci_post_xcodebuild.sh warns when an archive ran without it).
//   - Hand archives: prefix the `xcodebuild archive` command (docs/TESTFLIGHT.md).
//     Xcode's Product > Archive does not read it unless Xcode itself was
//     launched with the variable set.
//   - GitHub CI's Release build, so the Pulse gate inspects what ships.
//
// Release and Beta only. Debug, tests, and `swift test` stay at their defaults.
SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL[config=Release] = -Osize
SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL[config=Beta] = -Osize
